WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[theme music playing]

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:07.358 --> 01:08.568
So your point is?

01:08.651 --> 01:09.986
I know what I want.

01:10.487 --> 01:12.697
I've thought of something
I don't want taken from me.

01:12.781 --> 01:13.907
Especially by death.

01:14.491 --> 01:15.325
Huh?

01:16.159 --> 01:16.993
Death?

01:17.786 --> 01:19.329
I'll make my second wish.

01:19.412 --> 01:20.413
Hold your horses.

01:21.998 --> 01:24.084
Think about it before you make your wish.

01:24.167 --> 01:26.795
Take a calm, hard look
at your deepest desires.

01:27.378 --> 01:29.964
Do you really want it enough
to sell your soul?

01:33.426 --> 01:36.471
Make my grandma young.

01:36.554 --> 01:37.889
The same age as me.

01:39.015 --> 01:39.849
This

01:40.892 --> 01:42.519
is my second wish.

01:42.602 --> 01:44.646
[intriguing music plays]

01:44.729 --> 01:45.563
[scoffs softly]

01:45.647 --> 01:48.483
But not right away,
because the cremation's tomorrow.

01:49.943 --> 01:51.110
So make it happen

01:51.694 --> 01:52.904
exactly 72 hours from now.

01:54.906 --> 01:56.825
You're scheduling your wish?

02:01.371 --> 02:02.205
Hawaii?

02:02.288 --> 02:04.415
Yes. Let's go to Hawaii together.

02:04.499 --> 02:06.459
In three days. For a change of scenery.

02:06.543 --> 02:09.045
Three days?
But if we're traveling so far, we'd need--

02:09.129 --> 02:11.798
I've made all the preparations.
You just need to show up.

02:12.549 --> 02:14.926
I've already bought the tickets.
Non-refundable.

02:15.009 --> 02:16.511
Already? Oh my.

02:16.594 --> 02:18.179
Then I'd better…

02:18.888 --> 02:21.432
Well, we wouldn't want these
to go to waste.

02:22.142 --> 02:24.018
We have no choice but to go.

02:24.102 --> 02:25.061
Goodness me.

02:25.145 --> 02:28.022
Is this real or just a dream?

02:28.106 --> 02:30.775
So go and brag to all the other grannies.

02:30.859 --> 02:32.610
Tell everyone in the village, okay?

02:33.528 --> 02:34.404
All right.

02:35.071 --> 02:35.905
CHEONGPUNG VILLAGE HALL

02:35.989 --> 02:36.823
[Heung-rye] Hawaii?

02:36.906 --> 02:38.074
Yes.

02:38.158 --> 02:39.951
I insisted it wasn't necessary,

02:40.034 --> 02:42.829
but my Ka-young
had already bought the tickets.

02:42.912 --> 02:44.998
She said I needed a change of scenery.

02:45.081 --> 02:46.416
I couldn't exactly say no.

02:46.499 --> 02:50.253
Surely she can't be making
that much money from an auto shop.

02:50.336 --> 02:52.589
I guess she saved everything she could.

02:52.672 --> 02:53.965
Oh boy. [chuckles]

02:54.048 --> 02:56.342
You must be cashing in
all your luck late in life.

02:56.426 --> 02:57.802
I'm so jealous.

02:57.886 --> 02:59.095
So when do you leave?

02:59.178 --> 03:01.097
You'll need to pack some kimchi
and side dishes.

03:01.180 --> 03:02.557
The day after tomorrow.

03:02.640 --> 03:06.269
I was actually thinking of heading
to the market today to make preparations.

03:06.352 --> 03:08.396
Do you need any groceries or anything?

03:08.479 --> 03:10.607
She's actually going to Seoul later today.

03:10.690 --> 03:12.650
For your doctor's appointment, remember?

03:12.734 --> 03:16.237
You're always telling me
to go to the doctor.

03:16.321 --> 03:18.740
None of you kids ever mention Hawaii.

03:18.823 --> 03:19.908
[Da-jin] All right.

03:19.991 --> 03:22.035
[clapping] Let's get started
with today's class.

03:22.118 --> 03:25.830
All together now.
Stretch it out, nice and long.

03:25.914 --> 03:27.123
Stretch.

03:27.206 --> 03:28.333
[Da-jin] To the right.

03:28.416 --> 03:29.626
[Pan-geum] To the right.

03:31.377 --> 03:33.504
-Branch Manager Kang.
-[line ringing]

03:33.588 --> 03:34.839
Hello, Manager Kang.

03:35.423 --> 03:38.301
Apparently, Ka-young is taking
Pan-geum to Hawaii.

03:39.135 --> 03:42.096
She's had a tough life,
but her later years are treating her well.

03:42.597 --> 03:45.767
If you want to go,
you could go with your son.

03:46.976 --> 03:49.562
[laughs] Goodness, there's no need.

03:49.646 --> 03:51.898
I shouldn't waste
what little money he earns.

03:51.981 --> 03:54.192
-[sighs]
-[line rings, stops]

03:54.275 --> 03:56.611
I'll prepare for the rites
with your sister-in-law,

03:56.694 --> 03:58.488
so don't you worry.

03:58.571 --> 04:00.823
-[line ringing]
-All right.

04:01.491 --> 04:03.284
I can't attend anyway.

04:03.868 --> 04:05.954
I have to go to Seoul to see Jeong-hwa.

04:06.496 --> 04:09.457
Why? Did something happen to her?

04:09.540 --> 04:11.542
[line ringing]

04:15.004 --> 04:16.005
[Im-seom] Where are you?

04:16.089 --> 04:18.925
[Jeong-hwa] Where else?
I'm at the college exam prep academy.

04:19.008 --> 04:22.762
I'm at your place right now.
Do you really think I didn't check there?

04:22.845 --> 04:23.888
[Jeong-hwa sighs]

04:23.972 --> 04:25.139
I'm canceling your lease.

04:25.223 --> 04:27.433
Did you keep me away
just to start this crap?

04:28.351 --> 04:31.729
[inhales, shouts] Do you know
what the hell I just found here?

04:31.813 --> 04:33.064
[Jeong-hwa] You're such a pain!

04:33.147 --> 04:34.816
Who are you to snoop around my room?

04:34.899 --> 04:35.984
I'm your mom.

04:36.526 --> 04:38.152
Do you even go to class?

04:38.236 --> 04:40.363
[Jeong-hwa] Right,
I wanted to talk to you about that.

04:40.446 --> 04:43.157
I'm not taking the college exams
or going to college.

04:43.241 --> 04:46.077
[scoffs] You're not going to college?

04:47.912 --> 04:49.998
What could you do without a degree?

04:50.873 --> 04:51.708
Tell me.

04:52.250 --> 04:54.085
What is it? [loudly] Go on, tell me!

04:54.168 --> 04:56.087
I can make it big without a degree!

04:56.170 --> 04:57.422
Do you even realize

04:57.505 --> 05:00.508
-just how much of a miracle this is--
-[Jeong-hwa] I'm hanging up!

05:00.591 --> 05:03.094
-[line disconnects]
-Hello? [breath shaking]

05:03.177 --> 05:05.054
[sobs, yells] Yoo Jeong-hwa!

05:05.888 --> 05:07.640
Why is this happening?

05:08.141 --> 05:10.893
Seriously… [sobbing]

05:12.103 --> 05:14.105
[crying]

05:15.565 --> 05:16.482
[sniffles]

05:21.321 --> 05:23.489
We used to be so close…

05:25.616 --> 05:27.827
when I was a supermarket cashier.

05:30.496 --> 05:31.539
My daughter and I.

05:32.040 --> 05:34.000
[Iblis] If you miss those times,
simply go back.

05:36.711 --> 05:38.463
You still have one last wish.

05:39.130 --> 05:40.882
I'm saying you can take it all back.

05:41.424 --> 05:43.426
[ominous music plays]

05:45.094 --> 05:46.095
[sniffles]

05:51.059 --> 05:52.852
I can't use it like that.

05:55.396 --> 05:56.856
It'd be a waste.

05:59.567 --> 06:00.443
I know.

06:01.903 --> 06:02.779
[chuckles softly]

06:03.905 --> 06:07.992
-[watch ticking]
-1,247 seconds, 1,248 seconds,

06:08.076 --> 06:11.329
1,249 seconds, 1,250 seconds.

06:16.793 --> 06:18.377
What the… Why isn't he showing up?

06:20.046 --> 06:23.174
-What is he doing?
-[wind whooshing]

06:25.051 --> 06:26.761
[exclaims, groans]

06:27.637 --> 06:30.014
Can't you tell the time?
Ever heard of being punctual?

06:30.098 --> 06:32.433
Ten seconds to go for my wish.
Is it done or not?

06:32.517 --> 06:33.351
[scoffs]

06:35.061 --> 06:36.437
Can't you tell the time?

06:37.063 --> 06:40.942
-We still have three seconds.
-[watch ticking]

06:43.111 --> 06:44.445
[alarm chimes]

06:44.529 --> 06:46.531
[energy surges]

06:47.782 --> 06:50.368
[suspenseful music plays]

06:50.451 --> 06:53.704
[Iblis] Your second wish
has also been fulfilled.

07:01.462 --> 07:03.631
-Grandma?
-[cell phone clatters]

07:05.258 --> 07:08.553
[Pan-geum] Gosh, what time is it?
Is it already time to go to the airport?

07:10.471 --> 07:13.015
I haven't even finished packing yet.

07:14.350 --> 07:15.768
[groans]

07:15.852 --> 07:17.895
What's this? How did this come undone?

07:20.106 --> 07:21.023
[sighs]

07:22.191 --> 07:24.569
We should take some gochujang
and kimchi, right?

07:24.652 --> 07:26.654
[music intensifies]

07:30.867 --> 07:31.784
Grandma.

07:33.119 --> 07:34.287
You were this pretty?

07:34.370 --> 07:35.580
What are you saying?

07:36.205 --> 07:38.708
I'm all puffy because I crashed
right after eating.

07:39.625 --> 07:41.127
[clears throat]

07:41.836 --> 07:42.920
What's with my voice?

07:43.004 --> 07:45.590
You're so much prettier
than I imagined you'd be.

07:45.673 --> 07:46.799
It's too early for that.

07:47.675 --> 07:51.512
Who do you think you got those looks from?
You got them from me. [chuckles]

07:52.305 --> 07:55.057
[groans] Let's see.

07:55.808 --> 07:59.061
Shouldn't we at least boil some eggs
to eat before we go?

08:00.062 --> 08:02.273
[gasps] Goodness me.

08:03.024 --> 08:04.942
Who is that? Is she a friend of yours?

08:05.026 --> 08:07.445
No. You know Min-ji's my only friend.

08:07.528 --> 08:09.155
Then who is that?

08:12.492 --> 08:14.452
I swear I recognize her from…

08:16.370 --> 08:18.039
She looks so familiar…

08:18.122 --> 08:20.124
[suspenseful music plays]

08:21.626 --> 08:22.543
What the…

08:24.378 --> 08:25.421
Is…

08:26.506 --> 08:28.049
Is this a dream?

08:28.132 --> 08:29.258
Something like that.

08:29.759 --> 08:31.135
Do you know who it is now?

08:34.472 --> 08:36.474
[breath trembling]

08:37.058 --> 08:38.601
[gasping]

08:40.811 --> 08:42.396
I know who this is.

08:43.773 --> 08:46.984
This sprightly little thing is…

08:47.068 --> 08:49.445
-[gasping]
-[Ka-young] Oh.

08:50.488 --> 08:52.949
If you're going to faint,
fall to your left.

08:56.953 --> 08:58.162
[sighs]

09:00.373 --> 09:03.918
This young lady, who once pranced around
with the whole town at her fingertips, is…

09:04.001 --> 09:05.294
[sighs, thuds]

09:07.171 --> 09:09.924
If I wore some designer clothes
from Ka-young's wardrobe

09:10.424 --> 09:12.134
and some of her pointy heels…

09:15.137 --> 09:18.474
Goodness gracious. Dear Lord. Buddha.

09:18.558 --> 09:20.851
Gods of heaven and earth. Virgin Mary.

09:20.935 --> 09:24.564
Thank you. [wails, thuds]

09:26.482 --> 09:27.984
It wasn't any of them.

09:29.151 --> 09:31.279
-Think more Middle East.
-[chuckles]

09:33.281 --> 09:35.533
I've figured it out. It was that thing.

09:35.616 --> 09:37.577
Your notebook. Those wishes.

09:38.411 --> 09:39.996
-That's right.
-Really?

09:40.079 --> 09:44.125
So there's no going back, right?
[pants, chuckles]

09:45.251 --> 09:46.919
Uh-- [grunts]

09:48.671 --> 09:50.172
Oh. [gasps excitedly]

09:51.882 --> 09:53.593
What do you want with my room?

09:54.343 --> 09:55.553
Which one is Chanel?

09:56.137 --> 09:58.389
-[gasping]
-[hangers clattering]

09:59.515 --> 10:01.517
[cawing]

10:05.521 --> 10:07.273
[cawing continues]

10:07.356 --> 10:08.190
Really?

10:09.317 --> 10:11.986
So a lot happened overnight
in this tiny village.

10:15.406 --> 10:16.407
[grunts]

10:19.952 --> 10:22.913
Is it me, or have you been working out
unusually hard these days?

10:22.997 --> 10:25.958
It seems I'll be spreading my wings
more often. [grunts]

10:27.960 --> 10:29.420
They keep tearing my clothes.

10:29.503 --> 10:31.631
So you intend to fly naked?

10:31.714 --> 10:34.008
7,000 liters of water
go into making one garment.

10:34.967 --> 10:37.511
So you're actually going to fly naked?

10:37.595 --> 10:40.473
[exhales] Well?
Do you have something to report?

10:41.140 --> 10:43.392
Ms. Ki Ka-young has now made
her second wish.

10:43.476 --> 10:44.769
A righteous one at that.

10:44.852 --> 10:46.020
Congratulations.

10:47.021 --> 10:49.690
Good intentions don't always lead
to good outcomes.

10:50.316 --> 10:51.776
We can't let our guard down.

10:53.402 --> 10:54.779
Where is Iblis?

10:55.738 --> 10:56.864
[Iblis] Yeah, what?

10:56.947 --> 10:58.324
Making her grandma young?

10:58.407 --> 11:01.160
What about it?
You call that righteous? [scoffs]

11:04.330 --> 11:05.289
It's fine.

11:05.956 --> 11:07.375
Don't sweat the small stuff.

11:07.458 --> 11:10.086
Just look at Kang Im-seon's eyes.
Perfectly wicked.

11:11.587 --> 11:12.505
Hey.

11:13.089 --> 11:14.131
You're the best.

11:15.675 --> 11:17.760
But why do you keep sitting like this?

11:17.843 --> 11:18.886
My damn back.

11:20.179 --> 11:22.598
[groaning loudly]

11:28.854 --> 11:30.856
[tense music plays]

11:30.940 --> 11:33.859
Why are you intruding
on someone else's lamp?

11:33.943 --> 11:36.487
Did you make an appointment
when you crashed my rooftop?

11:38.489 --> 11:40.282
So Irem sang like a canary again.

11:40.908 --> 11:44.954
Hey. I get you're excited
that Ki Ka-young made a righteous wish,

11:45.037 --> 11:48.416
but her first wish was enough
for me to slit her throat.

11:48.499 --> 11:51.085
-[whines mockingly]
-So, one who was born on Wednesday,

11:51.168 --> 11:54.213
don't interrupt my precious contemplation
and get lost, will you?

11:54.296 --> 11:58.592
[laughs] Contemplation, my ass.
You were rattled and talking to yourself.

11:58.676 --> 12:00.302
Satan, who was born on Thursday.

12:00.386 --> 12:03.681
Rattled? Me? [laughs]

12:03.764 --> 12:05.182
You don't have a clue.

12:05.266 --> 12:07.184
Once you see Gu Bo-gyeong
and Eom Sang-tae…

12:07.268 --> 12:10.646
Oh. It's written all over their faces.
They will be corrupted.

12:10.729 --> 12:11.897
Oh, and the mutt?

12:11.981 --> 12:14.608
Come on, you already know.

12:15.109 --> 12:17.111
I said stop disrupting the human world.

12:17.194 --> 12:19.613
If a dog becomes a man,
is that the end of it?

12:19.697 --> 12:22.575
What about people's memories
if someone becomes young overnight?

12:22.658 --> 12:24.577
Gold and riches? You know it won't work.

12:24.660 --> 12:27.872
You can't deposit over ten million
without providing a source!

12:27.955 --> 12:29.874
Your methods? They're so old-school.

12:29.957 --> 12:33.002
You no longer have a use in this world.

12:33.085 --> 12:34.378
Even so,

12:35.045 --> 12:36.213
how could you say such…

12:37.590 --> 12:39.258
You're gassing me, you know.

12:39.341 --> 12:41.093
-"Gaslighting."
-[hesitates]

12:42.136 --> 12:43.637
Sade, that jerk!

12:45.431 --> 12:48.267
What will you do
if I prove that I do have a use?

12:48.350 --> 12:51.187
-[sighs]
-[man] Mr. Genie?

12:51.770 --> 12:53.105
Where are you?

12:53.189 --> 12:54.565
-[sighs]
-[man] Mr. Genie.

12:54.648 --> 12:55.983
Do your best to prove it, then.

12:56.650 --> 12:58.903
Everyone will start seeking you out now.

12:59.778 --> 13:01.655
As long as you're not seeking me out.

13:02.490 --> 13:04.325
Yes, I'm coming, Mutt.

13:04.867 --> 13:06.118
Where are you right now?

13:06.202 --> 13:08.037
[whooshes]

13:10.581 --> 13:14.752
Help me live
like an actual person. [panting]

13:14.835 --> 13:16.337
I look like a person.

13:16.837 --> 13:19.298
But as for what I can do… [sniffs]

13:19.840 --> 13:21.091
[in English] Nothing. [exhales]

13:21.175 --> 13:22.593
[in Korean] I can't do anything.

13:22.676 --> 13:23.594
[in English] You know?

13:23.677 --> 13:25.346
[in Korean] That's your second wish?

13:25.429 --> 13:27.014
It's the same as your first.

13:27.097 --> 13:30.351
What's with the manner of speech?
[laughs] Is it a shtick?

13:30.434 --> 13:31.810
[in English] No, no, no.

13:31.894 --> 13:33.020
[in Korean] My dad

13:33.604 --> 13:34.939
was a foreign dog.

13:35.022 --> 13:36.273
Anyway,

13:36.357 --> 13:39.193
I need money. And ID.

13:39.777 --> 13:42.655
-I must have money and ID.
-[sighs]

13:45.574 --> 13:47.535
I also find modern society so hard.

13:48.786 --> 13:50.996
And I suddenly have five wish-makers.

13:51.830 --> 13:52.748
[sniffing]

13:54.667 --> 13:56.710
I'm just as baffled as you.

13:57.211 --> 13:59.171
All right. How about this?

14:00.172 --> 14:02.216
I'll turn you into someone
who doesn't need ID.

14:02.299 --> 14:05.886
What kind of person would that be?

14:05.970 --> 14:07.596
The kind of person who pays

14:08.973 --> 14:10.558
to hire people who do have IDs.

14:10.641 --> 14:12.142
[chimes]

14:12.226 --> 14:16.063
GOBLIN STATIONERY

14:16.814 --> 14:18.983
[Iblis] The key here is wet hair.

14:19.567 --> 14:22.987
A man who'd rather boil to death in a suit
steps out of the driver's seat.

14:23.070 --> 14:24.905
[upbeat music plays]

14:25.489 --> 14:26.907
And you? Ha!

14:27.408 --> 14:28.659
You're in the back seat.

14:32.329 --> 14:33.664
Hey. Look over there.

14:33.747 --> 14:35.416
-Where?
-Damn.

14:35.499 --> 14:37.167
Looks like the fucking top dog.

14:37.710 --> 14:40.254
How did that motherfucker
end up with a car like that?

14:40.337 --> 14:41.755
[sighs] I'm damn jealous.

14:41.839 --> 14:43.591
He probably worked like a dog.

14:43.674 --> 14:46.218
I wish I had a dogshit ton of money
to flaunt too.

14:48.596 --> 14:50.598
[growls]

14:56.395 --> 14:57.688
[student] He's coming this way.

14:57.771 --> 14:59.940
[clicking tongue] Hey, you punks.

15:02.109 --> 15:06.280
You once kicked a dog
in this alleyway, didn't you?

15:06.363 --> 15:08.616
Are you familiar with cocker spaniels?

15:08.699 --> 15:10.951
You mean one of the top three
unhinged breeds?

15:11.535 --> 15:15.247
-So, what if we are? Oh, are you that dog?
-[chuckles]

15:16.540 --> 15:20.044
Then I guess you know
why I'm doing this too? Hmm?

15:20.920 --> 15:22.755
-[snarls]
-[student 1] The hell?

15:22.838 --> 15:24.214
[student 2] Hey, are you okay?

15:24.298 --> 15:27.176
-[student 1] This motherfucker!
-[student 2] You crazy fuck!

15:28.510 --> 15:29.845
Hey, you son of a bitch!

15:29.929 --> 15:32.056
-[growling]
-[yelping]

15:37.061 --> 15:39.063
-[panting]
-[student 2 panting]

15:41.523 --> 15:42.942
For your troubles.

15:43.025 --> 15:45.486
And don't ever mess with dogs again.

15:46.737 --> 15:48.989
I'll be watching you. [snarls]

15:49.073 --> 15:51.325
[student 1] Hey. The money.
Pick up the money.

15:51.408 --> 15:52.785
-Just pick it up already.
-[growls]

15:55.788 --> 15:57.039
[sighs heavily]

16:03.754 --> 16:04.588
Damn it.

16:04.672 --> 16:06.215
-[keypad beeping]
-[safe clanks opens]

16:13.222 --> 16:17.309
[Iblis] I can't believe your passcode
is actually 1004. [cackles]

16:18.060 --> 16:20.187
[tense comical music plays]

16:23.774 --> 16:25.192
[Ejllael] Damn it.

16:28.112 --> 16:32.533
[shouts] Iblis, you satanic asshole!

16:33.200 --> 16:35.828
-[door slams]
-[running footsteps]

16:36.870 --> 16:38.038
Grandma?

16:41.083 --> 16:41.959
Grandma?

16:49.466 --> 16:50.968
[gasps, sighs]

16:55.014 --> 16:56.140
[muttering]

16:56.682 --> 16:59.685
[sighs] A leather jacket in this heat?

17:00.227 --> 17:02.229
[peppy music plays]

17:03.188 --> 17:05.190
[humming]

17:08.736 --> 17:10.237
[gasps, exhales]

17:17.453 --> 17:18.537
Chanel.

17:20.539 --> 17:21.373
[grunts]

17:22.666 --> 17:25.461
Mmm! [giggles softly]

17:36.972 --> 17:37.806
[loudly] Grandm…

17:39.933 --> 17:42.019
-[grunts]
-[giggles softly, gasps]

17:45.272 --> 17:46.148
[clears throat]

17:47.941 --> 17:48.817
[scoffs]

17:48.901 --> 17:51.153
[peppy music continues]

17:52.279 --> 17:53.989
[pants, exclaims]

17:56.116 --> 17:57.076
[exhales]

18:02.748 --> 18:05.209
I'm not out of breath.
Not even close to exhausted.

18:05.959 --> 18:07.336
My hip is like new.

18:08.253 --> 18:09.880
[gasps excitedly, chuckles]

18:11.131 --> 18:13.008
-[squealing]
-[gasps]

18:16.512 --> 18:18.931
-[giggling, gasping]
-[motorbike whirring]

18:19.640 --> 18:20.682
Grandma, watch out!

18:22.559 --> 18:23.727
[gasps]

18:24.603 --> 18:25.646
[chuckles]

18:32.069 --> 18:32.903
You good, son?

18:34.863 --> 18:36.990
You should respect your elders,
young lady.

18:37.491 --> 18:40.035
"Young lady"? [laughs excitedly]

18:40.119 --> 18:41.161
"Young lady"?

18:41.829 --> 18:44.623
[squeals, chuckles] "Young lady"!

18:44.706 --> 18:46.333
-[whooping]
-[scoffs]

18:47.668 --> 18:49.419
[comical music plays]

18:49.503 --> 18:50.587
[humming]

18:54.675 --> 18:56.468
Uh…

18:56.552 --> 18:57.970
[exclaiming excitedly]

19:04.184 --> 19:06.895
[Ka-young] Grandma's going to need
some rules too.

19:07.396 --> 19:08.272
Mmm.

19:08.355 --> 19:10.357
[Pan-geum humming]

19:13.193 --> 19:15.070
-Ooh.
-Aren't you hot?

19:17.030 --> 19:17.990
[Pan-geum] No way.

19:18.073 --> 19:20.075
I'm at the perfect temperature. Why?

19:20.159 --> 19:23.453
Everything I say now is a rule
you must follow, no matter what.

19:25.122 --> 19:27.124
First, never answer this phone.

19:27.207 --> 19:29.835
Never. Not with this new
nightingale voice of mine.

19:29.918 --> 19:31.503
I won't answer.

19:31.587 --> 19:33.380
New cell phone, okay. What else?

19:33.463 --> 19:34.673
By the way…

19:34.756 --> 19:36.758
Second, if anyone asks why you're here?

19:36.842 --> 19:38.427
For a six-month countryside stay.

19:38.510 --> 19:39.720
Third. From where?

19:42.055 --> 19:43.724
-Hadong?
-Hey, Ki Ka-young?

19:43.807 --> 19:45.976
But Hadong's out in the country too.

19:46.059 --> 19:48.312
Say you're from Cheongdam, Seoul.
And your name…

19:48.395 --> 19:49.354
I already picked one.

19:49.438 --> 19:51.565
Lee Mi-ju. Suits me, doesn't it?

19:51.648 --> 19:54.484
Great. Fourth.
Drop that dialect from now on.

19:55.068 --> 19:57.654
This is between him, you, and me.

19:57.738 --> 20:00.616
So you need to stick to the rules
and not get caught. Got it?

20:00.699 --> 20:03.535
Come on, now.
Do you think I'm some nitwit?

20:03.619 --> 20:04.912
When I was young…

20:05.495 --> 20:07.664
Hold up, I am young now.

20:07.748 --> 20:11.835
The thing is, I just want to know
what's on the menu for dinner tonight--

20:11.919 --> 20:14.254
You don't even need to eat.
Why are you pigging out?

20:15.005 --> 20:17.299
-Grandma. Use a Seoul dialect.
-[tuts]

20:19.426 --> 20:20.844
Goodness gracious!

20:20.928 --> 20:22.554
That scared the daylights out of me!

20:23.430 --> 20:24.514
[clears throat]

20:25.599 --> 20:28.352
Oh, sorry. That freaks me out every time.

20:28.435 --> 20:30.395
Anyway, when I was young,

20:30.479 --> 20:32.814
I was also pretty chic and had big dreams

20:32.898 --> 20:36.777
Ah. Do you still need to go to the salon
to enter the Miss Korea pageant?

20:36.860 --> 20:38.904
You have a monolid.
You wouldn't make the cut.

20:38.987 --> 20:42.366
Don't think about anything else.
Just go and do something about your hair.

20:42.950 --> 20:44.743
Shouldn't I get eyelid surgery first?

20:45.786 --> 20:47.579
So stingy about food.

20:48.163 --> 20:50.457
I don't even eat that much. [scoffs]

20:52.251 --> 20:54.544
Gosh, this young man sure got here early.

20:54.628 --> 20:57.464
He looks strong too.
He'll probably get picked first.

20:57.547 --> 20:59.841
Move over a little. Scooch over.

20:59.925 --> 21:02.010
-Thanks.
-Go on, scooch over.

21:02.094 --> 21:04.054
[man] There you go. That's it.

21:04.137 --> 21:06.473
-Wait, I…
-Just a little more. That's it.

21:06.556 --> 21:07.766
They'll fall off.

21:08.308 --> 21:10.477
Okay, I need people
to work the cabbage patch.

21:10.560 --> 21:11.853
First 15.

21:11.937 --> 21:14.022
-Me!
-Hey, me!

21:14.106 --> 21:16.525
What are you doing?
Are you all uncomfortable?

21:17.484 --> 21:18.860
Me too!

21:18.944 --> 21:21.363
I'm very uncomfortable. Me!

21:21.446 --> 21:22.322
[man] Here, me!

21:22.406 --> 21:23.949
I'm extremely uncomfortable!

21:26.493 --> 21:29.538
[man humming, mumbling]

21:40.340 --> 21:42.301
[energetic music plays]

21:42.384 --> 21:43.552
[Iblis grunting]

21:47.222 --> 21:48.974
[man 1] Come and have your meals!

21:49.057 --> 21:50.350
Enjoy your meals.

21:50.434 --> 21:52.894
-[man 2] I know, right?
-Did someone go buy rice wine?

21:52.978 --> 21:55.147
-[man 3] He's on his way to buy it.
-Right away?

21:55.230 --> 21:56.732
-[man 3] He's off to get it.
-[grunts]

21:56.815 --> 21:57.858
Wow, this is…

21:57.941 --> 22:01.111
-[man 4] Goodness, thank you.
-[man 5] Oh, thank you.

22:01.194 --> 22:03.280
[indistinct chatter]

22:04.072 --> 22:05.782
Eating without paying? Seriously?

22:06.825 --> 22:10.370
Thanks to you,
we can call it a day now. [chuckles]

22:10.454 --> 22:11.455
-Hmm?
-Here.

22:12.914 --> 22:14.624
-What is this?
-[man] Your pay for the day.

22:16.293 --> 22:17.210
I get paid too?

22:17.794 --> 22:19.921
-[man laughs]
-Huh?

22:20.005 --> 22:21.798
-[man 2] Thank you. [laughs]
-Incredible!

22:23.467 --> 22:24.968
[man 1] I thought I was going to die.

22:25.052 --> 22:27.387
[man 2] You here? Go on, sit.

22:28.263 --> 22:29.639
Scooch over. Come on.

22:32.142 --> 22:33.518
-Hey.
-You're here again!

22:33.602 --> 22:34.561
Hi, Mr. Kim.

22:39.608 --> 22:41.234
-[light thuds]
-[tires screech]

22:41.318 --> 22:43.320
-[squeaks]
-[engine whirring]

22:48.909 --> 22:50.911
[breathing laboriously]

23:03.715 --> 23:04.925
[Sang-tae] What is this?

23:08.678 --> 23:10.472
[deer breathing laboriously]

23:13.016 --> 23:15.519
What a fucking pain in the ass.

23:17.395 --> 23:19.106
You should have just died.

23:21.525 --> 23:22.818
-[wind whooshes]
-[grunts]

23:22.901 --> 23:24.903
[wind blowing]

23:28.240 --> 23:29.616
Who are you?

23:29.699 --> 23:31.034
Where did you come…

23:35.705 --> 23:36.581
Did you see that?

23:36.665 --> 23:39.960
Yes, I saw it all.
But that's not important.

23:40.544 --> 23:43.421
I am Genie, the lamp spirit.
I shall grant you three wishes.

23:43.505 --> 23:45.090
No reviving or going to the future.

23:45.173 --> 23:48.135
Anything besides that,
your wish is my command.

23:48.969 --> 23:51.054
Mister, are you drunk or something?

23:51.138 --> 23:53.265
Just go on your merry way.

23:53.348 --> 23:55.976
And know you're only alive
because you're a guy.

23:57.435 --> 23:58.395
You can see me?

23:58.478 --> 24:00.355
Man, I was in a rush and came as myself!

24:00.438 --> 24:03.483
I was first in line too.
Now hurry, what's your first wish?

24:03.567 --> 24:05.402
[scoffs] What a joke.

24:06.194 --> 24:08.488
Who the fuck let this moron
out this early?

24:08.572 --> 24:09.990
You're a genie?

24:10.991 --> 24:12.284
Then bring this back to life.

24:12.826 --> 24:14.035
[intriguing music plays]

24:14.119 --> 24:16.413
Thank you so much for your prompt wish.

24:16.913 --> 24:19.457
It's possible
because it's still breathing. Mmm.

24:20.167 --> 24:22.127
[chiming]

24:26.715 --> 24:27.757
[bellows]

24:30.802 --> 24:31.803
[Iblis] Look at it go.

24:31.887 --> 24:34.723
Shall we keep it rolling
and get to your second wish?

24:35.390 --> 24:38.476
[yells] Fuck!

24:38.560 --> 24:40.770
[inhales] This is real?

24:40.854 --> 24:43.440
[loudly] That's seriously fucked up!

24:43.523 --> 24:46.776
[pants, yells] You should have told me
that it was real!

24:46.860 --> 24:50.614
I just blew a wish on nothing,
you motherfucker!

24:51.531 --> 24:54.201
-[panting]
-[engine revving]

24:55.243 --> 24:56.411
-[tires screech]
-[yelps]

24:56.494 --> 24:57.495
[metal clanks]

24:58.121 --> 25:00.123
[suspenseful music plays]

25:05.378 --> 25:06.630
You fucking moron.

25:08.089 --> 25:10.759
If you're a genie,
that makes me your master.

25:10.842 --> 25:12.052
Treat me like it, damn it!

25:12.135 --> 25:14.888
Why should I? That's a misconception.

25:14.971 --> 25:17.641
I may grant wishes,
but I can also have a nasty temper.

25:21.019 --> 25:21.978
Like this.

25:23.104 --> 25:25.649
[Sang-tae grunts, groans]

25:26.233 --> 25:31.696
[groaning] Just a moment. Please.

25:32.572 --> 25:35.742
So that means
I have two wishes left, right? [panting]

25:45.126 --> 25:47.921
Wait, where did the lamp go?
Why can't I see it?

25:48.004 --> 25:51.424
The lamp will appear when you desire
something enough to wish for it.

25:52.300 --> 25:54.678
Give it careful thought
before summoning me.

25:54.761 --> 25:57.681
And don't bother trying to control me,
you lowly human.

25:58.265 --> 26:02.352
Ah. And there's no point
trying to remember my face.

26:03.103 --> 26:05.188
I'll look different to you anyway.

26:05.855 --> 26:07.065
[laughs cunningly]

26:12.946 --> 26:16.199
Fucking piece of shit!

26:16.283 --> 26:18.618
[music intensifies, fades]

26:18.702 --> 26:20.120
[Da-jin] Good morning, Homies!

26:20.203 --> 26:23.164
We're up early today
to plant some lettuce.

26:23.248 --> 26:25.583
A lot of you struggle with insomnia,
don't you?

26:25.667 --> 26:27.210
I have bad insomnia too.

26:27.711 --> 26:29.337
So I'll grow these and "roar!"

26:29.421 --> 26:31.047
Gobble them all up.

26:31.131 --> 26:35.719
All right, lettuce seedlings
need to be planted 20 centimeters apart.

26:35.802 --> 26:37.971
Let's plant one here, and…

26:39.306 --> 26:40.849
Another one over here.

26:42.350 --> 26:43.393
One here.

26:45.645 --> 26:46.479
Oh…

26:46.563 --> 26:47.564
YOU'RE GOING TO KEEP ME UP AT NIGHT!

26:47.647 --> 26:48.648
YOU'RE KILLING ME!
ZOOM IN MORE!

26:48.732 --> 26:52.569
I think we'll end today's live here.
See you again when the lettuce has grown!

26:52.652 --> 26:55.572
Hey, what? Why are you… [sighs]

26:56.573 --> 26:59.326
-What was that? They were loving it!
-[deep sigh]

26:59.409 --> 27:00.994
-You zoomed in again, didn't you?
-What?

27:02.495 --> 27:05.457
Well, you know, you leaned over,
and I was just filming.

27:05.540 --> 27:08.543
-[chuckles, groans]
-What did you say? You sick bastard.

27:09.669 --> 27:11.546
Here. I present to you my left cheek.

27:13.006 --> 27:16.801
Come on, they say
to love thy enemies. Mmm.

27:18.511 --> 27:21.973
-You sly dog. You deserve a smack!
-Hey, come on. Quit it!

27:22.640 --> 27:25.435
[Sade] I've looked into it,
and you know that sleazy guy?

27:25.935 --> 27:29.314
This country has a university
that's really good in terms of science.

27:29.397 --> 27:31.358
That's where the two met.

27:31.441 --> 27:35.862
-Really? What did they do?
-[panting]

27:36.446 --> 27:37.989
They were in the waltz club.

27:38.823 --> 27:39.741
What?

27:41.368 --> 27:42.702
Waltz?

27:43.453 --> 27:45.455
[waltz music playing]

27:54.297 --> 27:55.298
How unexpected.

27:55.799 --> 27:57.926
I didn't think you'd be into waltzing.

27:58.009 --> 27:59.677
I wasn't interested at first,

27:59.761 --> 28:02.430
but a hometown friend of mine
suggested it,

28:02.514 --> 28:04.641
saying it's better
to break down beats than heads.

28:04.724 --> 28:05.850
[laughs]

28:06.935 --> 28:08.728
You sure are quirky.

28:09.270 --> 28:12.732
By the way, I saw you turned down
the President's Scholarship again.

28:12.816 --> 28:17.278
Thanks to you, I get to study abroad.
Maybe a research lab in the Arab League.

28:17.362 --> 28:18.196
Thanks.

28:18.279 --> 28:19.614
Don't mention it.

28:19.697 --> 28:22.242
I'm loaded, so I could pay
for the trip myself.

28:22.325 --> 28:26.162
Didn't you say you were from a small town
somewhere in Chungcheong-do?

28:26.246 --> 28:27.956
Our chili crops are booming.

28:31.251 --> 28:33.753
Man, you're so… [laughing]

28:36.423 --> 28:38.425
[waltz music continues]

28:42.053 --> 28:44.055
[music slows, stops]

28:44.139 --> 28:45.765
-I'm the best here, right?
-Yeah.

28:45.849 --> 28:47.684
-[whooshes]
-[grunts, thuds]

28:48.893 --> 28:49.936
[groans in pain]

28:50.019 --> 28:52.063
-Are you okay?
-There's nothing there.

28:52.147 --> 28:53.523
-[man 1] What's with you?
-Damn it.

28:53.606 --> 28:54.482
[man 2] What's wrong?

28:54.566 --> 28:56.609
You sure did fall over
in a very quirky manner.

28:56.693 --> 28:58.445
-What's gotten into you?
-What is it?

29:00.739 --> 29:02.574
Is your face okay?

29:02.657 --> 29:03.992
That's where you fell, right?

29:04.075 --> 29:05.118
Who is this bastard--

29:05.201 --> 29:08.121
Come on, you're hurt.
Don't bother trying to answer.

29:08.204 --> 29:11.416
Does it hurt a lot?
Did you break this bone here?

29:11.499 --> 29:13.835
-[muffled groaning]
-[cracking, snaps]

29:14.878 --> 29:16.880
[waltz music paying]

29:31.227 --> 29:32.187
[knock on door]

29:34.814 --> 29:35.648
We have guests.

29:40.737 --> 29:41.738
[Chang-sik clears throat]

29:46.284 --> 29:48.328
[Jong-heon] What's with this savage place?

29:49.746 --> 29:51.289
Will you even get a word in?

29:51.372 --> 29:53.500
It sure seems like… How should I put it?

29:53.583 --> 29:55.043
Not like an ordinary home.

29:55.126 --> 29:57.003
Right. It really does draw you in.

29:57.587 --> 29:59.130
Don't be a scaredy pants.

29:59.714 --> 30:00.548
Right.

30:01.174 --> 30:02.884
You sure have a large family.

30:02.967 --> 30:04.844
What? Are you all brothers?

30:04.928 --> 30:07.806
How patriotic of your parents.
Are we still waiting on the adults?

30:07.889 --> 30:08.890
Can I help you?

30:10.308 --> 30:13.186
Right, I guess introductions
are a little overdue.

30:13.269 --> 30:15.814
I'm the chief of Cheongpung Village--

30:15.897 --> 30:17.524
I asked if I can help you.

30:17.607 --> 30:18.942
[ominous music plays]

30:19.025 --> 30:21.486
Well, we heard you'd moved in,

30:21.569 --> 30:23.488
but you haven't shown your face.

30:23.571 --> 30:26.491
You need to complete resident forms,
but we didn't bring enough.

30:26.574 --> 30:28.785
We didn't know your family was so large.

30:28.868 --> 30:31.788
Local village news is posted regularly
on the Band channel,

30:31.871 --> 30:33.832
so make sure you're subscribed.

30:35.458 --> 30:36.626
Punch your number in.

30:38.294 --> 30:41.881
Goodness, I'm so forgetful.
I almost waited to ask you next year.

30:41.965 --> 30:43.800
-Your name is?
-It's Jung Jun-u.

30:43.883 --> 30:46.511
Hey, give him your number.

30:46.594 --> 30:48.596
[ominous music continues]

30:53.852 --> 30:55.728
I wasn't done talking over here…

31:02.485 --> 31:03.319
Mmm?

31:05.947 --> 31:06.948
What was that?

31:15.331 --> 31:16.499
What are you doing?

31:16.583 --> 31:17.709
Protecting Grandma.

31:19.210 --> 31:22.589
It all rides on keeping this quiet.
See if the screen's getting an image.

31:23.590 --> 31:24.591
Is that your third wish?

31:24.674 --> 31:26.426
If you're not going to help, piss off.

31:27.010 --> 31:28.177
Oh!

31:28.970 --> 31:30.179
Is that your third wish?

31:32.473 --> 31:34.058
Why are you on about wishes again?

31:35.101 --> 31:38.229
I grew up to be so pretty with no scars.

31:41.482 --> 31:43.318
When I was eight,
you told me not to get hurt.

31:45.528 --> 31:47.071
Haven't you heard of white lies?

31:47.155 --> 31:50.325
All lies are bad.
They steal chances to grow.

31:50.408 --> 31:54.495
Oh. Is that why you're working so hard
to install security cameras?

31:54.579 --> 31:56.623
Because you're so honest,
Ki Ka-young? [scoffs]

31:57.165 --> 31:59.167
[whooshes]

32:15.350 --> 32:16.476
[tools clattering]

32:17.060 --> 32:19.687
Hey, why aren't you barking at me? Huh?

32:24.150 --> 32:27.820
[Mi-ju grunts] I swear this is the spot.
Where is it?

32:29.739 --> 32:30.990
Darn it.

32:33.576 --> 32:35.411
-The money isn't there.
-[gasps]

32:35.495 --> 32:36.955
It hasn't been for ten years.

32:37.038 --> 32:38.373
You startled me, you brat.

32:38.998 --> 32:40.917
I nearly had a heart attack.

32:41.000 --> 32:43.670
-Unlikely. Your heart's young now.
-[exhales]

32:43.753 --> 32:46.339
I dug up all the money you buried
and donated it.

32:47.298 --> 32:48.132
What?

32:49.342 --> 32:50.677
How did you know about it?

32:50.760 --> 32:53.262
Wait. All of it? There was so much.

32:54.263 --> 32:56.683
-Just the starting amount.
-Just the starting amount?

33:02.105 --> 33:03.898
So you made some money off it?

33:03.982 --> 33:06.150
Hand it over. Let's split it 50-50.

33:06.234 --> 33:09.570
Even grandparents get paid
to babysit these days, you know.

33:09.654 --> 33:11.823
Half would be way too much.

33:13.157 --> 33:14.993
I've made a killing with it in stocks.

33:15.785 --> 33:16.703
Stocks?

33:18.579 --> 33:19.956
That thing you had me sign?

33:21.249 --> 33:23.418
[Min-ji] Aggressive investing
as a mere high schooler?

33:26.754 --> 33:30.133
[exhales] I saw all the stocks
you bought skyrocketing

33:30.216 --> 33:32.301
and thought you were
possessed or something.

33:32.385 --> 33:35.179
But then you used that money
to pay my college tuition,

33:35.263 --> 33:37.724
and you became a god-like figure
to my mom.

33:37.807 --> 33:39.934
I thought to myself,
"You're actually someone's god."

33:40.018 --> 33:40.935
"How awesome."

33:41.019 --> 33:44.856
"I'm finally escaping this town.
How exciting!"

33:44.939 --> 33:45.940
Are you done eating?

33:46.774 --> 33:49.485
It just came out, so of course not.
Not by a long shot.

33:50.862 --> 33:53.573
What are you staring at anyway?
Is something going on?

33:53.656 --> 33:54.907
I want to hurry home.

33:54.991 --> 33:55.950
Why?

33:56.492 --> 33:57.577
Because of that jerk?

33:57.660 --> 34:00.830
I told you not to get too serious
with some jerk you don't know.

34:02.165 --> 34:04.834
Hey, what are you doing here?

34:04.917 --> 34:07.420
Didn't you go to Hawaii with Pan-geum?

34:07.503 --> 34:09.380
[tense music plays]

34:09.464 --> 34:12.216
Uh, something came up, so I couldn't go,

34:12.300 --> 34:14.302
but Grandma didn't want
to waste the ticket.

34:14.385 --> 34:17.847
She went on her own so she wouldn't waste
the swimsuit she'd bought.

34:17.930 --> 34:18.973
Alone?

34:20.683 --> 34:23.478
And why isn't she answering her phone?

34:23.561 --> 34:27.607
It's a long flight, a different time zone,
and with no roaming, no news is good news.

34:27.690 --> 34:30.860
Grandma went to Hawaii? Alone?

34:31.611 --> 34:34.655
Goodness, she's always so damn tactless.

34:34.739 --> 34:37.075
You could've given me the spare ticket.

34:37.658 --> 34:40.328
What use is an unused ticket? [tutting]

34:40.411 --> 34:42.288
Pack up a large to go for me.

34:42.371 --> 34:45.625
That one's just incapable
of thinking about others.

34:45.708 --> 34:47.376
No wonder no one speaks well of you.

34:47.460 --> 34:48.711
Right. To go.

34:49.754 --> 34:51.380
I'll get the rest of this to go.

34:51.964 --> 34:54.383
-I'll eat this at home.
-Then what about me?

34:54.884 --> 34:56.761
I'm still eating.

34:56.844 --> 34:59.222
SOYEON SALON

34:59.806 --> 35:03.935
-[sighs] Mmm.
-[scooter approaching]

35:04.018 --> 35:05.353
Move!

35:05.436 --> 35:08.064
-[Min-ji] Hey, watch out!
-[exclaims]

35:08.898 --> 35:10.900
-[gasps]
-[serene music playing]

35:15.446 --> 35:18.491
Hey, jackass! It's illegal
to ride scooters on sidewalks!

35:18.574 --> 35:21.202
-I saw your face, you know.
-[chuckles]

35:22.453 --> 35:23.287
Are you all right?

35:23.371 --> 35:25.123
Goodness me, young lady!

35:25.206 --> 35:28.000
Min-ji, you really take no nonsense…

35:31.045 --> 35:32.255
do you, miss?

35:33.297 --> 35:35.133
-Do you know me?
-Uh…

35:36.759 --> 35:39.387
You own the dental clinic over there.

35:39.929 --> 35:41.097
You're quite famous.

35:42.181 --> 35:46.185
I'm Lee Mi-ju, and I'm here
for a six-month countryside stay.

35:46.269 --> 35:49.939
I read Smile Dental Clinic's a must
when visiting Cheongpung,

35:50.022 --> 35:52.024
so I was just thinking
about when to go. [laughs]

35:52.108 --> 35:54.402
You were? [chuckles]

35:54.485 --> 35:55.653
Please do. Come whenever.

35:56.237 --> 35:59.448
But judging by that smile just now,
you don't have any teeth to fix.

35:59.532 --> 36:03.494
[gasps] Holy smokes.
My teeth must have gotten younger too.

36:03.578 --> 36:05.705
You must be from Gyeongsang-do.

36:06.247 --> 36:08.166
Where are you staying?

36:08.833 --> 36:12.295
Well, I… [chuckles]

36:12.879 --> 36:16.340
[inhales] I'm sure we'll bump
into each other again, don't you think?

36:16.424 --> 36:17.842
If fate would have it.

36:17.925 --> 36:19.927
[chuckles] Well, sure.

36:20.678 --> 36:22.889
And if you're going to get your hair done…

36:22.972 --> 36:24.765
You have an excellent jawline,

36:24.849 --> 36:27.894
so a simple blowout
could add some character

36:27.977 --> 36:29.020
while keeping your volume.

36:30.229 --> 36:31.105
[chuckles softly]

36:37.486 --> 36:38.779
[sighs in relief]

36:40.323 --> 36:43.034
A blowout?
Does she realize how much that costs?

36:43.534 --> 36:46.120
I could do that myself at home.
Why would I come to a salon?

36:48.331 --> 36:49.540
Shall we, then?

36:59.342 --> 37:01.052
I heard you have something to say.

37:01.552 --> 37:02.720
It's nothing major.

37:03.638 --> 37:06.098
You were classmates
with Ms. Ki Ka-young, right?

37:07.350 --> 37:08.768
We weren't close, so…

37:09.268 --> 37:11.020
[girl] What's for lunch today?

37:11.103 --> 37:13.064
[indistinct chattering]

37:13.147 --> 37:16.609
[manager] You may not have been close,
but you're not complete strangers, right?

37:18.486 --> 37:20.029
Must I really spell it out?

37:20.112 --> 37:22.865
Do I really need to be doing this?
I should be home by now.

37:22.949 --> 37:26.786
All right, look.
You know our new pension package?

37:26.869 --> 37:30.081
The only VIP we have
who can comfortably afford that package

37:30.164 --> 37:32.083
is Ms. Ki Ka-young, you know?

37:32.166 --> 37:35.503
You could go and see her
and do some… you know?

37:35.586 --> 37:37.797
Can't you take some initiative
for a change?

37:38.631 --> 37:40.007
I'll think about it.

37:40.091 --> 37:43.219
Now is not the time
to say you'll think about it!

37:43.302 --> 37:46.222
I've already done
all the thinking for you.

37:46.847 --> 37:50.476
Work it out over the weekend, all right?

37:51.936 --> 37:52.770
[clears throat]

37:54.438 --> 37:55.731
[door opens]

37:55.815 --> 37:57.483
[somber music plays]

37:57.566 --> 37:58.567
[door closes]

37:59.068 --> 38:01.070
[breath trembling]

38:01.904 --> 38:02.738
[inhales]

38:04.824 --> 38:05.908
[deep sigh]

38:20.881 --> 38:23.175
[scoffs] A kettle?

38:26.429 --> 38:29.515
Who the hell used this thing
that's a bitch to clean?

38:31.767 --> 38:33.519
-[chimes]
-[exclaims]

38:33.602 --> 38:37.398
[yelping] What is this?

38:37.481 --> 38:40.109
[coughing] Is this micro dust or what?

38:42.987 --> 38:44.989
[enchanting music plays]

38:51.454 --> 38:54.248
I am Genie, the lamp spirit.

38:55.041 --> 38:57.668
I shall grant you three wishes. Make them.

38:58.586 --> 38:59.920
No bringing back the dead.

39:00.755 --> 39:02.006
No traveling to the future.

39:02.590 --> 39:04.342
-Anything besides that--
-A genie?

39:04.425 --> 39:05.426
Mmm?

39:07.887 --> 39:10.014
-Wait, I'm not quite done explain…
-[chuckles]

39:11.057 --> 39:13.059
[laughing maniacally]

39:18.230 --> 39:20.483
I honestly had faith, you know.

39:20.983 --> 39:24.028
I truly believed
that a day like this would come.

39:24.111 --> 39:26.322
I haven't had such a quick response
in some time.

39:26.405 --> 39:28.032
I'll make a wish.

39:28.115 --> 39:29.283
For my first wish…

39:30.368 --> 39:32.745
Ki Ka-young, she runs an auto shop.

39:35.039 --> 39:36.582
[music intensifies]

39:36.665 --> 39:37.500
And?

39:38.042 --> 39:41.045
GU BO-GYEONG
JUNE 20, 2024

39:41.128 --> 39:43.464
MADE HER FIRST WISH

39:44.298 --> 39:46.592
All right. What was Gu Bo-gyeong's wish?

39:48.135 --> 39:50.179
Tell me quick. I need to go get a refund.

39:50.930 --> 39:53.557
-I'm even dressed for the occasion.
-Dressed for a refund?

39:53.641 --> 39:56.102
I got a used spanner set,
but the fourth one's missing.

39:56.185 --> 39:58.604
I really like the number four. [inhales]

39:58.687 --> 40:00.022
I won't allow it.

40:02.441 --> 40:04.443
Blood on white clothes.
Now that'd be pretty.

40:05.069 --> 40:06.487
So hurry up and tell me.

40:07.071 --> 40:08.656
What did Gu Bo-gyeong wish for?

40:10.574 --> 40:13.953
Give me all the money
that's in Ki Ka-young's account.

40:16.914 --> 40:18.916
You want to be rich like Ki Ka-young?

40:18.999 --> 40:20.376
No. That's not it.

40:20.876 --> 40:24.130
I want all the money
that's in Ki Ka-young's account.

40:26.048 --> 40:27.216
Every last cent.

40:27.758 --> 40:28.592
[exclaims]

40:30.219 --> 40:31.053
I see.

40:32.847 --> 40:34.849
You want Ki Ka-young's misfortune.

40:36.350 --> 40:37.184
Hmm.

40:38.227 --> 40:41.897
Ah. What should I do?

40:43.274 --> 40:45.276
[energy surges]

40:51.574 --> 40:52.408
It is done.

40:53.659 --> 40:54.577
Really?

40:55.536 --> 40:56.745
[cell phone chimes]

40:58.789 --> 41:01.417
DEPOSIT, KI KA-YOUNG
10,000,000 WON

41:01.500 --> 41:03.836
[screaming excitedly]

41:06.589 --> 41:07.882
And your second wish?

41:07.965 --> 41:09.884
Wait, just a moment.

41:09.967 --> 41:12.803
I don't have to make it right away, do I?

41:14.221 --> 41:16.348
[chuckles] For now…

41:18.809 --> 41:21.270
I just want to cherish this moment.

41:21.353 --> 41:23.355
[intriguing music playing]

41:28.694 --> 41:32.448
[Iblis] Ki Ka-young, who said humans
are kind, has appeared in another's wish.

41:32.531 --> 41:33.949
Still believe in humans?

41:34.033 --> 41:36.118
It does make me angry
how she singled me out.

41:38.162 --> 41:39.538
But a bet is still a bet.

41:42.374 --> 41:44.835
Kang Im-seon, Eom Sang-tae,
and Gu Bo-gyeong.

41:45.920 --> 41:47.796
I think I'll be winning this bet.

41:47.880 --> 41:51.759
WANTED EVERYTHING
IN KI KA-YOUNG'S ACCOUNT, EVERY LAST CENT

41:53.052 --> 41:53.886
Yes.

41:57.556 --> 41:59.391
It does seem to be heading that way.

42:02.728 --> 42:04.230
So just stay still.

42:08.275 --> 42:11.445
-[gentle ballad plays]
-[hesitates]

42:12.696 --> 42:13.989
What are you doing?

42:15.824 --> 42:18.494
You asked to be taken care of.
So I'm doing just that.

42:18.577 --> 42:20.120
I can't do this if I lose.

42:24.583 --> 42:26.710
Boy, my dear Lee Beul-li is warm.

42:27.962 --> 42:30.422
My darling Satan sure is warm.

42:32.841 --> 42:35.511
My dear Iblis is so warm.

43:00.828 --> 43:02.329
I've been curious for a while.

43:03.831 --> 43:06.959
Why doesn't that hourglass flow?
Doesn't that mean it has no purpose?

43:07.543 --> 43:09.295
Because it's a coffin, not a clock.

43:10.588 --> 43:11.922
That's you in there.

43:13.048 --> 43:14.717
I was locked up with a handful of you.

43:15.593 --> 43:16.427
A coffin?

43:17.011 --> 43:18.053
[grunts]

43:25.728 --> 43:29.356
Oh. So a coffin can actually be this tiny.

43:29.940 --> 43:32.985
Damn, I got mine
down to a size five Korea Post box.

43:33.736 --> 43:35.946
We were so warm just now.

43:36.447 --> 43:38.240
Are you seriously flash-freezing me out?

43:43.746 --> 43:45.247
[Ka-young] Did you hold rites for me?

43:45.331 --> 43:47.333
[chimes]

43:48.083 --> 43:50.085
[tense music plays]

43:55.466 --> 43:57.468
-Huh?
-[rapid ticking]

44:03.307 --> 44:04.308
[music swells]

44:04.391 --> 44:08.479
-[indistinct shouting]
-Cast the Goryeo bitch aside too!

44:08.562 --> 44:09.813
Please.

44:09.897 --> 44:11.440
[music intensifies]

44:11.523 --> 44:13.525
[laughing]

44:16.445 --> 44:17.279
[gasps]

44:22.618 --> 44:23.452
What is it?

44:24.328 --> 44:25.621
So it really was me.

44:26.246 --> 44:27.498
The laughing girl in my dreams.

44:29.375 --> 44:30.876
I've dreamed about this place.

44:32.628 --> 44:34.505
The decor is a little different,

44:35.673 --> 44:36.757
but it was definitely here.

44:39.593 --> 44:40.969
I was laughing here.

44:41.512 --> 44:42.888
What are you talking about?

44:43.389 --> 44:46.350
You've never been in here.
Not once in the past.

44:47.643 --> 44:48.977
Then did I see the future?

44:49.520 --> 44:50.604
It was definitely me.

44:51.522 --> 44:53.524
I was smiling. Like this.

44:57.444 --> 44:58.362
That creepily?

45:03.617 --> 45:05.285
Where did you hide my toolbox?

45:13.961 --> 45:15.337
You should've taken it in.

45:15.421 --> 45:17.089
Even if there are issues,

45:17.172 --> 45:19.383
I'll need to order parts,
so I can't fix it right away.

45:19.967 --> 45:21.677
It's all right. Just do a regular checkup.

45:23.262 --> 45:25.264
Wait here.
I need to go to the bank quickly.

45:31.603 --> 45:32.438
[objects clattering]

45:35.983 --> 45:36.859
Look away.

45:37.985 --> 45:39.862
-I don't like it when people watch me.
-[thuds]

45:40.487 --> 45:42.281
-[screeches]
-[thuds]

45:46.702 --> 45:49.705
Is it okay for an adult
to speak so harshly to a child?

45:49.788 --> 45:51.498
You think being young gives you a pass?

45:52.666 --> 45:54.543
Go sit over there and read your book.

45:55.085 --> 45:56.253
I've already finished it.

45:56.336 --> 45:57.171
HISTORY OF GORYEO

45:57.254 --> 46:00.674
In Goryeo times, Arabia was called
Saracen, and the two had close ties.

46:00.757 --> 46:03.510
But the exchanges stopped
after the year 1040.

46:04.094 --> 46:05.053
I wonder why.

46:05.137 --> 46:06.472
Did someone block the path?

46:06.555 --> 46:07.764
It wasn't me.

46:07.848 --> 46:10.184
Do you know "Twin Flower Shop"?
The Goryeo-era song?

46:10.267 --> 46:13.687
They say the foreign man in the song
was actually an Arabian merchant.

46:14.188 --> 46:16.356
If he came all the way to Goryeo
from Arabia,

46:16.440 --> 46:19.860
there must be people
who traveled from Goryeo to Arabia, right?

46:19.943 --> 46:22.029
Ask the Internet, not the auto shop.

46:22.112 --> 46:23.113
[distant footsteps]

46:23.697 --> 46:24.823
What is it now?

46:25.699 --> 46:26.950
[loudly] Hey, part-timer!

46:28.952 --> 46:30.078
Did you call me?

46:30.162 --> 46:31.538
Watch the shop for a bit.

46:31.622 --> 46:33.499
Those are some of my favorite heels!

46:39.922 --> 46:41.924
[mysterious music plays]

46:47.262 --> 46:48.096
[Mi-ju exclaims]

46:48.931 --> 46:49.765
Wait.

46:50.682 --> 46:51.517
[exhales]

46:58.065 --> 46:59.816
[pop music playing on speaker]

47:05.280 --> 47:06.156
Let's see.

47:09.493 --> 47:11.411
Come on. What's wrong with this thing?

47:11.495 --> 47:12.371
[mumbles]

47:12.454 --> 47:13.664
[serene music plays]

47:13.747 --> 47:15.874
If you're getting coffee, this one's good.

47:16.458 --> 47:19.127
So we did run into each other. Like fate.

47:19.211 --> 47:20.212
[chuckles softly]

47:20.295 --> 47:21.755
It's such a small town.

47:22.631 --> 47:23.840
You go first.

47:23.924 --> 47:25.676
So you weren't wondering what to drink.

47:26.385 --> 47:27.678
Haven't you used a kiosk before?

47:27.761 --> 47:29.346
Well, about that…

47:29.429 --> 47:31.223
So you always had someone
to do it for you?

47:31.890 --> 47:33.850
Who were the jerks who did it all for you?

47:34.643 --> 47:35.477
[giggling]

47:35.561 --> 47:37.479
This coffee tastes better
with an extra shot.

47:38.105 --> 47:39.481
[chuckles softly]

47:40.732 --> 47:41.775
Why are you laughing?

47:43.652 --> 47:46.071
Because I'm grateful, and you're cute.

47:46.154 --> 47:47.948
That's a pretty dangerous thing to say.

47:48.740 --> 47:50.867
You straightened your hair. It's pretty.

47:51.451 --> 47:53.996
[exclaims] It's not pretty at all.

47:54.079 --> 47:55.539
It's… Oh!

47:56.081 --> 47:58.542
Maybe it's because my clothes
are doing all the work.

47:59.042 --> 48:00.127
Your clothes

48:01.128 --> 48:01.962
are a no.

48:02.629 --> 48:04.006
What?

48:04.089 --> 48:05.090
[laughing]

48:09.386 --> 48:10.887
-[chuckles]
-[Mi-ju] Oh gosh.

48:11.722 --> 48:12.806
[Iblis] What are you doing?

48:13.473 --> 48:14.308
[distant laughter]

48:14.933 --> 48:16.810
[Ka-young] Keeping an eye on Grandma.

48:16.893 --> 48:18.437
But she keeps laughing.

48:18.520 --> 48:19.563
Look.

48:20.147 --> 48:21.315
True joy.

48:22.649 --> 48:23.483
Why is that?

48:24.318 --> 48:26.445
They grow up so fast. [tuts]

48:28.697 --> 48:29.823
Damn it.

48:30.782 --> 48:33.160
She should just live
with Min-ji, then. [tuts]

48:35.871 --> 48:36.830
[Iblis] By the way,

48:38.915 --> 48:40.792
about that thing where you show me care.

48:41.918 --> 48:43.420
What are the rules for that?

48:44.504 --> 48:46.548
Is it the time, the place,

48:46.632 --> 48:48.884
the day, or the outfit?

48:50.344 --> 48:51.428
Does it matter?

48:52.346 --> 48:54.598
I feel like trash, so don't talk to me.

49:00.187 --> 49:01.396
Come on.

49:09.905 --> 49:12.532
No, that's not it!

49:13.116 --> 49:13.950
Seriously.

49:16.536 --> 49:17.746
[yells] That's not it

49:18.246 --> 49:19.289
[sighs in annoyance]

49:19.873 --> 49:21.792
[angrily] Iblis!

49:22.376 --> 49:23.418
[grunts]

49:24.294 --> 49:25.879
[pants]

49:29.007 --> 49:30.842
Why aren't they coming out?

49:35.138 --> 49:35.972
[exhales]

49:37.307 --> 49:38.725
You, come with me.

49:38.809 --> 49:40.310
[Iblis exclaiming]

49:40.394 --> 49:41.353
[grunts]

49:42.354 --> 49:44.356
[instrumental music playing]

49:49.528 --> 49:50.362
[sighs]

49:54.199 --> 49:57.369
You completely emptied my safe

49:57.869 --> 49:59.413
and gave that huge amount of money

50:00.288 --> 50:01.248
to that mutt.

50:01.873 --> 50:03.834
You told me to consider modern systems.

50:05.293 --> 50:08.380
That was the only money that was free
from modern-day systems.

50:09.005 --> 50:10.298
And he's not a mutt.

50:11.299 --> 50:13.760
His dad's actually from England
and has quite the pedigree.

50:13.844 --> 50:15.053
[chuckles]

50:28.984 --> 50:30.444
Why gouge out the angels' eyes?

50:31.778 --> 50:34.406
Isn't that
how the painting was originally?

50:35.115 --> 50:36.783
Originally? [loudly] Originally!

50:37.576 --> 50:39.119
You know what it took to restore it?

50:40.787 --> 50:41.621
[sighs]

50:42.664 --> 50:43.874
I can't take it anymore.

50:45.250 --> 50:47.252
[suspenseful music playing]

50:48.712 --> 50:49.963
[grunts, exclaims]

50:51.923 --> 50:53.258
[exclaiming]

50:57.679 --> 50:58.513
Deary me.

50:59.639 --> 51:00.557
[laughs mischievously]

51:09.649 --> 51:10.734
[grunts]

51:11.693 --> 51:13.904
[both screaming]

51:37.677 --> 51:39.179
[Iblis] Game over.

51:39.721 --> 51:42.224
Ten, nine…

51:42.307 --> 51:43.517
[chuckles]

51:45.018 --> 51:46.603
[yells] Iblis!

52:00.075 --> 52:02.494
[laughing, giggling]

52:24.266 --> 52:25.475
Please.

52:26.643 --> 52:28.311
[Ka-young] What could it be? The sword?

52:28.854 --> 52:30.480
-Please.
-[Ka-young] The reaping hook?

52:30.564 --> 52:32.274
-Please.
-[Ka-young] The axe?

52:32.357 --> 52:33.483
Please.

52:36.695 --> 52:39.948
[Ka-young] I must have asked for a sword
that can cut a head clean off. Yes.

52:43.660 --> 52:45.662
[distant cawing]

52:50.125 --> 52:52.127
[crows cawing]

52:52.210 --> 52:54.212
[suspenseful music playing]

53:08.602 --> 53:10.437
Why would you come to my house?

53:11.813 --> 53:13.356
Don't tell me you came for my grandma.

53:14.733 --> 53:15.692
If so, you're dead.

53:15.775 --> 53:18.153
You may be the lamp's master,
but you can't kill me.

53:19.529 --> 53:21.948
-And I'm here to see you.
-Me?

53:23.909 --> 53:24.743
So I'm dying?

53:24.826 --> 53:26.661
[scoffs] Don't worry about that.

53:27.662 --> 53:29.331
Not for today, at least.

53:31.333 --> 53:33.543
I know you made your second wish.

53:36.254 --> 53:38.173
What does that have to do with you?

53:41.343 --> 53:43.178
I thought I might help you

53:44.179 --> 53:45.221
decide on your final wish.

53:45.305 --> 53:46.973
[intriguing music plays]

53:49.893 --> 53:52.312
Do you know the reason Iblis

53:53.271 --> 53:54.189
wants to kill you?

53:54.272 --> 53:56.232
Because I locked him up in his lamp.

53:56.900 --> 53:58.276
So he wants to get revenge.

53:58.360 --> 53:59.653
That's right.

53:59.736 --> 54:02.072
Then what might be the reason you died?

54:05.992 --> 54:07.118
Aren't you curious…

54:11.164 --> 54:12.666
about what happened?

54:14.292 --> 54:15.669
Won't you come with me…

54:18.463 --> 54:19.839
to the moment you died?

54:21.424 --> 54:23.426
[music intensifies]

54:33.311 --> 54:35.313
[rock fusion music plays]
